#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:13
msgid "Using variants - how-to"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:16
msgid ""
"Variants provide convenient installation groups for related ROS packages. "
"This article explains how official variants are defined and how to create "
"project-specific metapackages. After you read it, you can propose community "
"variants or build private variants for your own packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:26
msgid "Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:28
msgid ""
"Metapackages do not provide software directly but depend on a group of other "
"related packages to provide a convenient installation mechanism for the "
"complete group of packages. [#]_ [#]_ Variants are a list of official "
"metapackages for commonly useful groups of ROS packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:32
msgid "https://wiki.debian.org/metapackage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:33
msgid "https://help.ubuntu.com/community/MetaPackages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:35
msgid ""
"The different variants in ROS 2 are specified in `REP-2001 <https://reps."
"openrobotics.org/rep-2001/>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:37
msgid ""
"In addition to the official variants, there may be metapackages for specific "
"institutions or robots as described in `REP-108 <https://reps.openrobotics."
"org/rep-0108/#institution-specific>`_."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:40
msgid "Adding variants"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:42
msgid ""
"Additional variants that are of general use to the ROS community can be "
"proposed by contributing an update to `REP-2001 via pull request <https://"
"github.com/openrobotics/reps/blob/main/_posts/rep-2001.md>`_ describing the "
"packages included in the new variant. Institution and robot specific "
"variants can be published directly by their respective maintainers and no "
"update to REP-2001 is required."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:46
msgid "Creating project-specific variants"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:48
msgid ""
"If you are creating ROS packages to use privately in your own projects, you "
"can create variants specific to your projects using the official variants as "
"examples. To do so you need only create two files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:51
msgid ""
"A minimal variant package is created as a package with the ``ament_cmake`` "
"build type, a ``buildtool_depend`` on ``ament_cmake`` and ``exec_depend`` "
"entries for each package you want to include in the variant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:53
msgid ""
"<?xml version=\"1.0\"?>\n"
"<?xml-model href=\"http://download.ros.org/schema/package_format2.xsd\" "
"schematypens=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema\"?>\n"
"<package format=\"2\">\n"
"  <name>my_project_variant</name>\n"
"  <version>1.0.0</version>\n"
"  <description>A package to aggregate all packages in my_project.</"
"description>\n"
"  <maintainer email=\"maintainer-email\">Maintainer Name</maintainer>\n"
"  <license>Apache-2.0</license>\n"
"  <!-- packages in my_project -->\n"
"  <exec_depend>my_project_msgs</exec_depend>\n"
"  <exec_depend>my_project_services</exec_depend>\n"
"  <exec_depend>my_project_examples</exec_depend>\n"
"\n"
"  <export>\n"
"    <build_type>ament_cmake</build_type>\n"
"  </export>\n"
"</package>"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:73
msgid ""
"A minimal ament_cmake package includes a ``CMakeLists.txt`` which registers "
"the package.xml as an ament package for use in ROS 2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:75
msgid ""
"cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.20)\n"
"\n"
"project(my_project_variant NONE)\n"
"find_package(ament_cmake REQUIRED)\n"
"ament_package()"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:83
msgid ""
"You can then build and install your variant package alongside your other "
"private packages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:86
msgid "Creating custom variants with platform-specific tools"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/Developer-Tools/Build/Using-Variants.rst:88
msgid ""
"Some platforms have tools for creating basic packages that do not require a "
"full ROS build farm environment or equivalent infrastructure. It is possible "
"to use these tools to create platform-dependent variants. This approach does "
"not include support for ROS packaging tools and is platform dependent but "
"requires much less infrastructure to produce if you are creating collections "
"of existing packages rather than a mix of public and private ROS packages. "
"For example, on Debian or Ubuntu systems you can use the ``equivs`` "
"utilities. The Debian Administrator's handbook has a `Section on meta-"
"packages <https://www.debian.org/doc/manuals/debian-handbook/sect.building-"
"first-package.en.html#id-1.18.5.2>`_."
msgstr ""
